ce: Bhatia and Angelou 2015.\r\n","value":null,"unit":"W","appliance":"very_low_load","family":"rated_power_w"},"ev-3be5d8ed104e":{"type":"evidence","doc_id":"nrel_pue_microgrids_2018","page":6,"quote":"on weekdays between 9:00 AM and 5:00 PM","value":null,"unit":"hour of day","appliance":"grain_mill","family":"usage_window"},"ev-3bec9cd85733":{"type":"evidence","doc_id":"power_africa_pue_catalog_rwanda_2020","page":40,"quote":"Power (energy consumption) 70 W 100 W","value":70.0,"unit":"W","appliance":"refrigerator","family":"rated_power_w"},"ev-4837d07843b0":{"type":"evidence","doc_id":"unnamed","page":null,"quote":"In Kenya and Tanzania micro-grids, a table saw is rated 1,600–1,800 W on three-phase power, with start-up draw of 3,300–5,000 W [B].","value":null,"unit":"W","appliance":"table_saw","family":"rated_power_w"},"ev-4a43beddf08c":{"type":"evidence","doc_id":"unnamed","page":null,"quote":"**Power rating, no location (weak source):** A Quora answer uses 75 W as an *assumed* example for an electric sewing machine. This is not a spec sheet and doesn't meet your sourcing standard.","value":75.0,"unit":"W","appliance":"sewing_machine","family":"rated_power_w"},"ev-4f4b565e75b3":{"type":"evidence","doc_id":"unnamed","page":null,"quote":"In Kenya and Tanzania micro-grids, the illustrative \"carpentry tools\" business case uses 18 kWh per month [B].","value":18.0,"unit":"kWh/month","appliance":"carpentry_tools","family":"monthly_kwh"},"ev-5159a2922b8f":{"type":"evidence","doc_id":"nrel_pue_microgrids_2018","page":6,"quote":"at 33% loading (2.6 hours per day) or 50% loading (4 hours per day)","value":2.6,"unit":"h/day","appliance":"grain_mill","family":"hours_per_day"},"ev-536aa7d20bd6":{"type":"evidence","doc_id":"unnamed","page":null,"quote":"Hair dryers in Ugandan salons are rated from 500 W to 3,000 W, and 1,100 W is the most common rating. [1]","value":1100.0,"unit":"W","appliance":"hair_dryer","family":"rated_power_w"},"ev-5a63e322a24e":{"type":"evidence","doc_